/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (I am delighted to welcome the Cambridge Lucy India Futures Forum \(CLIFF\), an important initiative that strengthens the Collegiate University's engagement with India and complements the University's wider commitment to deepening partnerships through the Cambridge-India Centre for Advanced Studies \(CAS\). The launch of CLIFF reflects the strength and potential of the Cambridge-India relationship, building on a long shared history while creating new opportunities for collaboration, learning, and impact.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Cambridge Lucy India Futures Forum)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
137 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (In particular, I warmly welcome Lucy Cavendish College's commitment to fostering partnerships with Indian institutions and expanding opportunities for student and staff mobility. These efforts will help deepen academic exchange, support the development of new research and educational collaborations, and strengthen our engagement with India's rapidly evolving knowledge economy and higher education landscape. By bringing together students, academics, alumni, and partners, CLIFF has the potential to make a significant contribution to the next chapter of the relationship between Cambridge and India.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 59 0 R
/E (Professor Bhaskar Vira FAcSS)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
